    {
      "id": "step-vous-formal",
      "type": "theory",
      "title": "Tu or vous?",
      "body": "## The *tu* / *vous* choice\n\nFrench requires you to pick one of two forms for \"you\":\n\n| Situation | Use |\n|---|---|\n| Talking to one friend, family member, child | **tu** |\n| Talking to a stranger, customer, professor (one person) | **vous** |\n| Talking to more than one person, any formality | **vous** |\n\nNote that **vous** does double duty (formal singular AND any plural). The verb conjugation is the same, context tells you which one is meant.\n\nWhen in doubt with someone new, use **vous**. They'll let you know if it's OK to switch to **tu** (\"*on se tutoie*\", let's use tu).\n\nAt A1, when you don't know which to pick, **vous** is the safer choice."
    },
